WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.520
Just a few weeks shy of her&nbsp;
100th birthday, the iconic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:08.640
beloved, and groundbreaking Betty White&nbsp;
passed away, on December 31st, 2021.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.320
A few days before, on December 28th,&nbsp;
the actor took to Instagram to share&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.320
her latest cover of People magazine with&nbsp;
fans, the headline of which read "Betty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.240
White turns 100!" with a quotation&nbsp;
reading "Funny never gets old."

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.040
The magazine includes an exclusive&nbsp;
interview with the actress,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.640
which was one of White's last before her&nbsp;
passing, while also featuring several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.440
of White's friends — including actors Ryan&nbsp;
Reynolds, Carol Burnett, and Sandra Bullock.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:35.760
On top of that, the cover references the&nbsp;
legendary actor's "secrets for happiness."

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.440
Having lived for such a long time, White&nbsp;
witnessed plenty of change in the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.080
including the rise of social media, and she&nbsp;
adapted to everything with grace. Her Instagram&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:49.600
account has 1.9 million followers who eagerly&nbsp;
awaited any and all news White posted about.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.480
White's prolific portfolio of award-winning work,&nbsp;
her efforts as an animal rights activist, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:59.040
lasting impact she had in the world of comedy&nbsp;
will no doubt be celebrated for years to come,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:04.160
but her final Instagram post is causing its fair&nbsp;
share of heartbreak for her fans around the world.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.400
White captioned her last Instagram post,

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:11.360
"My 100th birthday… I cannot believe it is coming&nbsp;
up, and People Magazine is celebrating with me!"

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.480
In a matter of hours, the Dec. 28th post garnered&nbsp;
a large amount of likes and comments, and as one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:20.960
fan wrote in the wake of the news of her death,&nbsp;
"she is forever a golden girl in our hearts."

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:25.760
The ultimately heartbreaking post currently&nbsp;
sits at well over 600k likes and counting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:30.160
with a heartwarming comment from one&nbsp;
follower reading simply, "National treasure."

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:34.800
White's career spans nearly eight decades, and&nbsp;
in that time, the five-time Emmy Award-winning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.000
Illinois native also took on the&nbsp;
roles of writer and producer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.920
As an actor, she brought an endless list&nbsp;
of unforgettable characters to life.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:45.280
While her character on "Golden Girls"&nbsp;
is arguably her most well-known,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:48.880
she also made her mark with performances&nbsp;
in other projects like "Hot in Cleveland,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.120
"The Proposal," and "The Mary Tyler Moore Show."

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.960
In the People magazine feature, friend and&nbsp;
costar Sandra Bullock (who starred in "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.280
Proposal" with White) said she hoped White would&nbsp;
celebrate her birthday the same way she, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.200
"celebrated every day of her life with&nbsp;
humor, kindness and a vodka on ice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.880
toasting to the fact that she's a&nbsp;
badass who has left us all in the dust."

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:10.640
While the occasion is now much sadder than it&nbsp;
should have been, many people around the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:14.240
are still planning to celebrate the life of&nbsp;
Betty White on what would have been her 100th&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:19.600
birthday on January 17th, 2022. The plans&nbsp;
already in place include a documentary movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:24.000
special that will be in theaters for one night&nbsp;
only, called "Betty White: 100 Years Young."

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.880
A short trailer for the movie,&nbsp;
distributed by Fathom Events,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.360
includes clips from the entertainer's long career,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.840
as well as an invitation from White herself,&nbsp;
telling fans that "there is only one place to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.920
get the real Betty White," and that's here in&nbsp;
this movie. What better way to celebrate the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.000
life of Betty White than to spend January&nbsp;
17th celebrating with the woman herself?

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.720
The producers of the movie, Steve&nbsp;
Boettcher and Mike Trinklein,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:48.800
shared their thoughts about the prolific actress&nbsp;
in a statement after her death. They said,

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:52.400
"Betty always said she was the 'luckiest&nbsp;
broad on two feet' to have had a career as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.480
long as she did. And honestly, we were the&nbsp;
lucky ones to have had her for so long."

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.480
Clarifying their plans for the film, they stated&nbsp;
that the movie will still premiere as planned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.880
to, quote, "provide a way for all who loved her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:06.640
to celebrate her life — and experience&nbsp;
what made her such a national treasure."

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.880
The movie will highlight White's fantastic,&nbsp;
long career, including her final interview,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:15.440
and showcase the many friends who loved her so&nbsp;
much, including Ryan Reynolds, Carol Burnett,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:19.438
Robert Redford, Clint Eastwood,&nbsp;
Valerie Bertinelli, and many more.

